<title>LEBANON: Libano-Francaise bank capital increase approved.</title>
<headline>Libano-Francaise bank capital increase approved.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shareholders in Beirut's Banque Libano-Francaise voted on Tuesday to increase the bank's capital to 100 billion pounds ($64.8 million) from 60 billion, a bank executive said.</p>
<p>&quot;Shareholders agreed today to raise capital through the capitalisation of reserves and retained earnings,&quot; Maurice Kayrouz, Director of Merchant Banking, told Reuters.</p>
<p>($1 = 1,543.5)</p>
<p>- Beirut editorial (9611) 745308 602057 745307</p>
